  "support": {
    "status": "candidate",
    "since": "2026-11-11",
    "evidence": [
      "Live on 2026-11-11 on a Linux server installed from Steam at this build (all declared files match the pins) with this target's zip: the plugin loads under SourceMod 1.13 on server version 11191711, registers as a new game server with hosted Takaro on protocol 1, and a real Steam client (build 26334388) joins; getPlayers carries the Steam ids the server status shows, the join lands on the player's existing Takaro player, connect, disconnect, a console command and a server message work, again after a server restart and a client reconnect",
      "srcds_linux, srcds_run, bin/engine_srv.so and tf/bin/server_srv.so are byte-identical to the linux-25995664 pin; only tf/steam.inf (the version string) changed",
      "games/tf2/tests/validate-static.mjs (contract level, every build: action, event, cvar and wire-shape checks over the plugin source)"
    ],
    "notes": "The connector is a SourceMod plugin (takaro_tf2.smx) plus the ProjectSky websocket and json extensions; it holds the Takaro connection itself, no sidecar. It needs MetaMod:Source 1.12 and SourceMod 1.13 on the server (SourceMod 1.12 crashes current TF2 builds); neither is shipped in the zip. The plugin uses SourceMod's game-event and SDK APIs only, no code addresses, so a new TF2 build usually keeps working, but every build needs a live retest before it is declared."
  },
